"Make the db:start network-exposure check also probe non-internal IPv6 addresses. Today scripts/db/stack.ts (externalAddresses in defaultStackDeps, and findExposedPorts) only enumerates IPv4 addresses, so a machine with a LAN, private or global IPv6 address passes the check while the Supabase CLI ports (published on all interfaces) are reachable there. Skip link-local IPv6 addresses that need an interface scope, or probe them with their scope. Add unit tests with a fake IPv6 address that answers (refused) and none that answers (passes), update the code summary note and --help text if they mention IPv4 only, and keep the rule that DB_ALLOW_ALL_INTERFACES is set only by the owner. Source: finding R-01 (Major) of the U1 review; plan group A in aidlc/spaces/default/intents/261012-real-backend-local/follow-ups/minor-findings-plan.md."
